      "widgets_values": [
        "## Video is the main job here\n\nTopaz Video AI is a **video** product, and so is this pack. The examples start from\n`Load Image` only because a still is the quickest thing to try.\n\n**To run this on video, change the two ends:**\n\n| Replace | With |\n|---|---|\n| `Load Image` | `Load Video` -> `Get Video Components` (images / audio / fps) |\n| `Save Image` | `Create Video` (images + fps + audio) -> `Save Video` |\n\nEverything between them stays exactly as it is. Every Topaz node takes a plain IMAGE\nbatch and does not care where the frames came from.\n\nWire `fps` from `Get Video Components` into the Topaz node's `fps` widget and into\n`Create Video`, and pass `audio` straight across — the frames go through Topaz, the\nsound goes around it.\n\nSee `07_video_upscale.json` for that graph already built."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
